ant that was awarded a Michelin star for the period 2013–2019. Blok's was awarded a Bib Gourmand in the period 2007–2012. The sudden loss of the Bib in 2012 was a big shock and they did not understand it. Three weeks later the restaurant was awarded a Michelin star."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-blok-s-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blok's_Restaurant"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Fusion cuisine","links":[["Karen Keygnaert","dish/karen-keygnaert"],["Kojacha","dish/kojacha"],["Saucebox","dish/saucebox"],["The Peak Lookout","dish/the-peak-lookout"],["Variety Jones (restaurant)","dish/variety-jones-restaurant"]]}]},"ingredient/bilberry":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bilberry","n":"Bilberry","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Bilberry (), also known as European blueberry, is a Eurasian low-growing shrub in the genus Vaccinium of the flowering plant family Ericaceae. Vaccinium myrtillus L. is the species most commonly called bilberry, but other closely related Vaccinium species may also have this name."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bilberry"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilberry"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Blåbärssoppa","dish/blabarssoppa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bilberries","ingredient/bilberries"],["Potato starch","ingredient/potato-starch"],["Starch","ingredient/starch"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"dish/dong-an-chicken":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dong-an-chicken","n":"Dong'an chicken","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dong'an chicken is a Chinese cold parboiled chicken dish, flavoured with chili peppers, ground Sichuan peppercorns, white rice vinegar, scallions and ginger. It is named after Dong'an County."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dong-an-chicken"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dong'an_chicken"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["A+ Hong Kong Kitchen","dish/a-hong-kong-kitchen"],["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Chinese Tuxedo","dish/chinese-tuxedo"],["Chowking","dish/chowking"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Country Dough","dish/country-dough"],["Cuisine AuntDai","dish/cuisine-auntdai"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dim Sum King","dish/dim-sum-king"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Duck House Chinese Restaurant","dish/duck-house-chinese-restaurant"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Flower Drum","dish/flower-drum"],["Frank Fat's","dish/frank-fat-s"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Handpulled Noodle","dish/handpulled-noodle"],["Harbor City Restaurant","dish/harbor-city-restaurant"],["Heichinrou","dish/heichinrou"],["HK Cafe","dish/hk-cafe"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Hotcha (company)","dish/hotcha-company"],["House of Louie","dish/house-of-louie"]]}]},"ingredient/shaobing":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/shaobing","n":"Shaobing","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Shaobing, also called huoshao, is a type of baked, unleavened, layered flatbread in northern Chinese cuisine. Shaobing can be made with or without stuffing, and with or without sesame on top. Shaobing contains a variety of stuffings that can be grouped into two main flavors: savory or sweet. Some common stuffings include red bean paste, black sesame paste, stir-fried mung beans with egg and tofu, braised beef, smoked meat, or beef or pork with spices."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-shaobing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaobing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Donkey","ingredient/donkey"],["Donkey meat","ingredient/donkey-meat"]]}]},"ingredient/jackfruit":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/jackfruit","n":"Jackfruit","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["The jackfruit or jakfruit (Artocarpus heterophyllus) is a fruit tree in the mulberry family of Moraceae. Native to India, the species was first described under the name Artocarpus heterophyllus in Encyclopédie Méthodique, Botanique in 1789 by Jean-Baptiste Lamarck, based on a specimen collected by botanist Philibert Commerson."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-jackfruit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackfruit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Gudeg","dish/gudeg"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Gnetum gnemon","ingredient/gnetum-gnemon"],["Nangka","ingredient/nangka"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tempeh","ingredient/tempeh"],["Garcinia binucao","ingredient/garcinia-binucao"],["Pigeon pea","ingredient/pigeon-pea"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]}]},"dish/hash-stew":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hash-stew","n":"Hash (stew)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Southern American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Hash, often called pork hash or liver hash, is a name for a stew or gravy made of pork, offal and onions. It is usually paired with rice as \"hash and rice\". Hash is part of the cuisine of the Southern United States where it was invented as a way to use unappetizing cuts of meat. The dish is primarily consumed within the state of South Carolina, where it is commonly paired with barbecue. Many variations of hash exist, which include different combinations of meats and vegetables."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hash-stew"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hash_(stew)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southern-united-states"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Lana's Cooking","ref":"site/lanascooking-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lanascooking.com","note":"Lana Stuart's blog of Southern home cooking from Georgia.","url":"https://www.lanascooking.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"A Southern Soul: Southern Classics","ref":"site/asouthernsoul-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"asouthernsoul.com","note":"Collection of classic Southern recipes on a Southern home cooking blog.","url":"https://asouthernsoul.com/recipes/southern-classics","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Southern American cuisine","links":[["Ambrosia (fruit salad)","dish/ambrosia-fruit-salad"],["Barbecue bologna","dish/barbecue-bologna"],["Chess pie","dish/chess-pie"],["Chicken Maryland","dish/chicken-maryland"],["Chitlins","dish/chitlins"],["Conecuh Sausage","dish/conecuh-sausage"],["Fig (restaurant)","dish/fig-restaurant"],["Grape hull pie","dish/grape-hull-pie"],["Lambert's Cafe","dish/lambert-s-cafe"],["Lem's Bar-B-Q","dish/lem-s-bar-b-q"],["Lemon pepper wings","dish/lemon-pepper-wings"],["Mississippi mud pie","dish/mississippi-mud-pie"],["Monroe Sausage","dish/monroe-sausage"],["Moon Pie","dish/moon-pie"],["Paschal's","dish/paschal-s"],["Screen Door (restaurant)","dish/screen-door-restaurant"],["The Grey (restaurant)","dish/the-grey-restaurant"],["Yardbird Table & Bar","dish/yardbird-table-bar"]]}]},"dish/izumi-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/izumi-restaurant","n":"Izumi (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanes